# Corpus unit bridging-data-gaps/C03 — gap (comparative; resource_benchmarking_comparison -> controlled_comparison)
#
# Source: m0/annotations/bridging-data-gaps.yaml C03 (comparative; corpus pin 62e9b54). Headline:
# DDPM-TAN dominates full fine-tuning on FFHQ -> 10-shot Sunglasses across trainable params
# (1.3% vs 100%), iterations (300 vs ~5000), GPU-hours (3 vs 7.5), and peak memory (9 vs 20 GB),
# at equal-or-better FID.
#
# Lowering notes (conventions: corpus-units/LOWERING.md):
#   * Family map: resource_benchmarking_comparison -> controlled_comparison. This is a multi-metric
#     conjunction; modeled as one predicate over Q = training_resource_cost, with the per-metric
#     inequality chain and the FID-parity side condition folded into `nl` and refs.
#   * The annotation's mandatory CQ2 is unmet-gap: the two conditions run asymmetric configs
#     (baseline batch 5 / 1 GPU vs TAN batch 40 / 8x A100) that are never normalized, so the 9-vs-20
#     GB and 3-vs-7.5 GPU-h numbers are not comparable. Mapped onto policy-mandatory baseline_parity
#     -> unmet. The incomplete controlled_comparison argument is declared as a located hole with
#     `open baseline_parity` (lowering re-done for issue #15 under `lara-core@0.3`): it is not an
#     AF node, so the claim lands `gap` on empty complete support.
#   * CQ1 (FID at convergence equal-or-better, so resources are not traded for quality) discharges
#     the optional scope_match; the resource metrics themselves are recorded for both methods
#     (E03 steps 1-3), discharging measurement_validity. Both leaves are on the page.
#   * variance_reported also has no leaf (single measurement per config, no repeats) — a second
#     policy-mandatory blocker, also opened; baseline_parity is the annotation-grounded driver.
#
# Expected verdict is at the bottom of this file (golden oracle).

artifact bridging-data-gaps at sha256:5325ea757258
policy corpus-v1
use backends [nd@1]

# --- The headline claim, stated but not assemblable at corpus-v1's evidential bar --------------

claim c03
  nl      = "DDPM-TAN dominates full fine-tuning on FFHQ to 10-shot Sunglasses: 1.3% vs 100% trained params, 300 vs ~5000 iters, 3 vs 7.5 GPU h, 9 vs 20 GB peak, at equal-or-better FID; the batch 40 / 8x A100 vs batch 5 / 1 GPU configs are never normalized"
  formal  = better(ddpm_tan, full_finetune, training_resource_cost, ffhq_sunglasses_10shot)
  binding = { author = m0-annotator, audit-status = unreviewed }

# --- Evidence leaves are present ... ------------------------------------------------------------

leaf e1 : reports(e03, compares(ddpm_tan, full_finetune, training_resource_cost, ffhq_sunglasses_10shot, favorable))
  kind       = observed
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E03, logic/experiments.md#E03-Setup, trace/exploration_tree.yaml#N11-N12, PAPER.md#overview]

leaf e2 : valid_measurement(training_resource_cost, e03)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E03-Procedure-steps-1-3]

leaf e3 : scope_matched(ddpm_tan, training_resource_cost, ffhq_sunglasses_10shot)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E03-Procedure-step-4, evidence/tables/table2_fid.md, evidence/figures/figure4_ablation.md]

# --- ... and the incomplete argument is declared as a located hole ------------------------------

# matched_setup(ddpm_tan, full_finetune, e03) has no honest leaf (asymmetric batch/GPU configs
# never normalized, CQ2) and variance_reported(e03) has none either (single measurement per
# config). Both are policy-mandatory and stay open: a1 is a hole, not an AF node.
arg a1 : supports(c03) by controlled_comparison(ddpm_tan, full_finetune, training_resource_cost, ffhq_sunglasses_10shot, e03)
  discharge measurement_validity with e2
  discharge scope_match          with e3
  open      baseline_parity
  open      variance_reported

status c03

# ==============================================================================================
# EXPECTED VERDICT (golden oracle)
# ==============================================================================================
# Compiled AF: no arguments.
# Located hole: a1 (open obligations [baseline_parity, variance_reported]; sources no attacks).
# Claim status:
#   c03 -> gap (empty complete support; statusC = Gap iff null claimSupport, spec §8 — the hole
#               is reported, not a node)
